opportunity='Free-throw attempt volume was used as the grouped-binomial denominator rather than as a predictor. Previous model-adequacy analyses indicated that attempt volume is informative about player-level shooting and opportunity structure. Consequently, the primary model should be interpreted as a working conditional association model rather than a complete generative model of shooting opportunity. Player-clustered uncertainty does not repair conditional-mean misspecification.'
complextext='More elaborate hierarchical joint models of free-throw opportunity and accuracy were investigated during model development. These models showed posterior predictive misspecification or weak identification among opportunity and player-level latent effects, with predictive checks withheld when sampling failed. They were therefore not used for primary scientific inference. Their adequacy failures remain part of the scientific history.'
selection=f"Usable-measurement coverage ranged from {vv('coverage_min'):.1f}% to {vv('coverage_max'):.1f}% across the approved season series. Measured players are not a random sample of all NBA players. Combine participation, measurement availability and completeness, NBA survival, playing opportunity and shooting opportunity may select the sample; the model does not correct this selection. Unmeasured skill, training and current role remain possible sources of confounding."
ident='Residual wingspan is time invariant, so its coefficient is identified between players. Repeated seasons provide additional outcome information and dependence-aware uncertainty, but not within-player exposure identification. Player clustering is not adjustment for player fixed effects or unmeasured player ability.'
prtext=f"The primary grouped-binomial estimate was beta={p['beta']:.8f} per residual inch (OR={p['odds_ratio']:.6f}); the 95% player-cluster CR1 interval was [{p['ci_low']:.8f}, {p['ci_high']:.8f}] and the two-sided p-value was {p['p']:.8f}. The player-bootstrap percentile interval was [{p['bootstrap']['percentile_CI'][0]:.8f}, {p['bootstrap']['percentile_CI'][1]:.8f}]. Both intervals describe uncertainty around the same original primary point estimate."
sample=f"The primary replication panel comprised {p['seasons']} seasons, {p['player_seasons']:,} player-seasons and {p['players']} accounting players. Of these, {p['positive_FTA_rows']:,} positive-FTA rows from {p['contributing_players']} players contributed {p['FTA']:,} attempts; {p['zero_FTA_rows']} zero-FTA rows remained in accounting. The 2013-14 development season was excluded."
j2text=f"Secondary beta-binomial robustness retained the original full-sample estimate beta={q['beta']:.8f} (OR={q['odds_ratio']:.6f}; rho={q['rho']:.8f}). Its remediated player-bootstrap 95% percentile interval was [{b['percentile_CI'][0]:.8f}, {b['percentile_CI'][1]:.8f}], with {b['failed']}/{b['replicates']} failures. Historical Stage 3J remains EXECUTION FAIL; the separate Stage 3J-R decision is NUMERICAL REMEDIATION PASS. J2 remains secondary."
losotext=f"Across all 13 chronological leave-one-season-out omissions, beta ranged from {l['min_beta']:.8f} to {l['max_beta']:.8f} (median {l['median_beta']:.8f}); there were {l['sign_reversals']} sign reversals. No single omitted season reversed the direction; this is sensitivity evidence within the same panel, not independent replication."
practical='Each additional inch of wingspan beyond that expected for height was associated with approximately 3% lower adjusted odds of a made free throw. Odds are not percentage points. This is a between-player association and does not represent changing one player\'s anatomy.'
source_text='Anthropometric records came from a pinned secondary archive and were corroborated against official NBA historical combine tables. In the predeclared validation sample, all 45/45 same-player, same-year barefoot-height and wingspan pairs agreed exactly. A broader historical census included 970 rows and 965 complete pairs with exact core agreement; the frozen geometric reference comprised 960 positive-ID participants. Later official combine validation covered 582 records, including 543 complete pairs and four versioned corrections. Analytical linkage used exact positive NBA IDs; source-table name corroboration did not authorize fuzzy analytical joins.'
