M('Study design','M01','Observational multiseason study of the adjusted association between residual wingspan and free-throw accuracy. The simplified analysis protocol was prospective to its own fitting, after earlier source audits and model-development analyses; it was not registration before all historical data inspection. '+ident,prot)
M('Data sources','M02','Pinned combine and player-game archives supplied measurements and regular-season shooting counts. Official NBA historical tables and selected official player/team records supported source validation. Source snapshots, retrieval metadata and checksums remain archived; no live-source refresh was performed for manuscript assembly.',[('docs/stage0c_anthropometric_validation.md','Sections 4-5,15,18'),('docs/stage3_evidence/shooting_archive_provenance.json','sources; manifests'),('docs/stage3b_protocol_amendment.md','Sections 3-8')])
M('Anthropometric measurements','M03','One fixed measurement vector per player was selected: the latest complete, plausible, officially supported, non-quarantined record on or before the start year of the first observed positive-minute NBA season in the archive. The first observed season may be left-truncated and is not necessarily the player\'s NBA debut. Barefoot height and wingspan use inches from the same record; no shoe-height substitution or outcome-guided measurement selection was used.',[('docs/stage3_multiseason_hierarchical_ft.md','Section 6')])
M('Exposure definition','M04',f"Residual wingspan = wingspan - ({vv('geometry_intercept')} + {vv('geometry_slope')} x barefoot height), in inches. The outcome-independent geometric reference fit was frozen in the development stage and reused unchanged. The reference included 960 usable positive-ID combine participants through 2013, regardless of NBA survival or FT attempts. Inference conditions on this fitted transformation and does not propagate its estimation uncertainty.",prot+[('docs/stage0c_evidence/validation_summary.json','reference_population')])
M('Free-throw outcome','M05','The grouped response was [FTM, FTA-FTM]. Makes and attempts were summed across recorded appearances; percentages were not averaged. Positive total season minutes defined eligibility. Recorded zero-minute appearances remained distinct from DNP/empty-minute records and contributed recorded counts.',prot+[('docs/stage3_multiseason_hierarchical_ft.md','Section 5')])
M('Study population','M06',sample,rep)
