M('Development vs replication split','M08','The 2013-14 season supplied development evidence. Primary replication used 2010-11, 2011-12, 2012-13 and 2014-15 through 2023-24. Players may overlap development data; the appropriate description is out-of-season replication or replication across additional seasons. The secondary full panel includes the development season and is not independent replication.',prot,split='development and replication explicitly separated')
M('Primary statistical model','M09','logit(p_it) = intercept + beta_RW residual_wingspan_i + beta_H barefoot_height_i + original_combine_position_i + season_t. Barefoot height remains in raw inches. Original hybrid categories remain distinct; missing position is unknown. C and 2010-11 are reference levels. The primary model has no player random intercept, player fixed effects, opportunity component, FTA predictor or MIN predictor. With mean misspecification, the coefficient is a working-logit projection dependent on the observed attempt and covariate distribution.',prot)
M('Player-cluster covariance','M10','Player scores are sums of grouped-row scores X_it(FTM_it-FTA_it*p_it). Sandwich covariance uses the inverse grouped-binomial information and player-summed outer products, with CR1 correction G/(G-1) x (N-1)/(N-K). Here G=835 contributing players, N=3,980 positive-FTA rows and K=28 estimable columns. Normal-Wald intervals and two-sided normal p-values were predeclared. Zero-only players supply no score clusters.',prot+[(J+'primary_result.json','covariance_validation.N; K; G')])
M('Player bootstrap','M11','The primary bootstrap used exactly 2,000 draws of 857 accounting players with replacement, carrying all seasons for each selected player and assigning duplicate copies distinct cluster identities. Zero-FTA rows remained in resampling accounting. No residualization was refitted. Percentile intervals used linear interpolation at the 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles. Bootstrap means are descriptive summaries; manuscript points remain the original fitted coefficients. Empirical fractions below zero are not posterior probabilities.',prot)
M('Robustness analyses','M12','The predeclared package retained beta-binomial regression with the same mean formula; earliest eligible replication season per player with HC1; player-balanced 1/T_i likelihood weights; FTA >=50 and >=100 subsets; each season omitted once; and a full secondary panel including 2013-14 development. T_i includes accounting seasons with zero attempts. Equal aggregate season weights do not equalize player information because attempt counts still differ. Alternate advantage and ratio exposures remain supplementary, with residual wingspan primary.',prot,role='secondary',split='replication; secondary full panel includes development')
sections[-1][1].append(P(name,'M13','The secondary beta-binomial player bootstrap required numerical remediation. A prospectively amended numerical ladder was applied uniformly to the exact original scheduled samples with the same likelihood, data and numerical acceptance gates. The original failed execution and the separate numerical-remediation pass are both disclosed. No failed-only percentile interval is used.',j2+[(JR+'numerical_protocol.json','algorithm and gates'),('docs/stage3jr_beta_binomial_numerical_remediation.md','Sections 5,8-12')],role='secondary'))
M('Missing / zero-attempt handling','M14','Incomplete or unsupported measurement pairs and unresolved name-only identity links were not admitted under frozen eligibility. Missing combine position is retained as unknown. No FT accuracy is imputed for zero attempts. Zero-FTA rows remain in accounting and bootstrap membership, while only positive-FTA rows inform the accuracy likelihood. In first-season sensitivity, an earliest eligible zero-attempt season is not replaced by a later positive season.',prot+[('docs/stage3_multiseason_hierarchical_ft.md','Sections 5-6')])
